<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Thracian Tomb of Sveshtari</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">3rd century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Thracian Tomb of Sveshtari is a royal tomb of the early 3rd century BCE near the village of Sveshtari in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a>. Its burial chamber has ten female figures carved in high relief, half human and half plant, supporting the roof, and a painted scene of a goddess crowning a horseman. It lies near Sboryanovo, often identified with the Getic royal city of Helis, and is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thracian-tomb-of-sveshtari.jpg" alt="Thracian Tomb of Sveshtari" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sveshtari_Thracian_tomb_Bulgaria_IFB.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
